course: dictionary
lesson: 13348
title: Hale and hearty
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words look ordinary but have two different uses. Hale is one of them. Most of the time it is an adjective that describes a person who is strong and healthy.
explain: «My grandad is still hale at eighty, and he walks to the shops every day.» Eighty is old, and he still walks every day, so hale must mean fit and well. People often say «hale and hearty» to mean the same thing, with hearty adding a sense of cheerful energy.
explain: Hale also has an old verb meaning. In old books, «He was haled into court» means he was pulled or dragged there, usually to be judged. You will mostly meet this in stories from long ago.
explain: Use the clues around the word. If the sentence is about someone being well and strong, use the first meaning. If it is about someone being pulled or dragged somewhere, the old meaning fits.
fact: Hale means strong and healthy, usually said about an older person.
fact: «Hale and hearty» means fit, well and full of energy.
fact: Hale can also be an old verb meaning to pull or drag someone, especially to court.
fact: «Haled» is the past tense of that old verb, as in «haled into court».
exercise: «The old farmer was hale, and he rode his horse every morning.» Find and copy the word that means strong and healthy. | morning | horse | *hale | rode
exercise: «Even at ninety, Granny Rose is hale and hearty.» What does hale mean here? | *Strong and healthy | Lost in the garden | Tired and sleepy | Very noisy
exercise: In an old story, «The guard haled the thief before the judge.» What does haled mean? | Cheered for | *Pulled or dragged | Gave a present to | Fell asleep
test: «My hale great-uncle still climbs the stairs without stopping.» What does hale tell you about him? | He is very small | He is very sad | He is lost | *He is fit and healthy
test: «The sailor was haled onto the ship by two strong men.» What does haled mean here? | Had a picnic on deck | Chose to sail away | Painted the ship | *Pulled or dragged onto the ship
exam: What does «hale and hearty» mean? | Tired after a long walk | Lost and cold | *Fit and well | Angry and loud
